# 7. Default backend: native PipeWire

PipeWire must be the default capture backend.

Use the **native PipeWire API**.

Do not make the default path:

```text
JACK API
    ↓
PipeWire JACK compatibility
```

and do not depend on JACK compatibility libraries.

The PipeWire backend should connect to the selected PipeWire MIDI source/port and consume MIDI control events directly from the PipeWire graph.

Example CLI:

```bash
midijitter record \
    --backend pipewire \
    --source "Scarlett 18i20 MIDI"
```

If no backend is specified:

```text
--backend pipewire
```

is implied.

