# 13. ALSA RawMIDI backend

Implement ALSA RawMIDI as an optional reference backend.

Example:

```bash
midijitter record \
    --backend alsa-raw \
    --device hw:1,0,0
```

This backend is useful for:

* measuring MIDI closer to the hardware/driver layer;
* comparing PipeWire timing with lower-level ALSA timing;
* diagnosing whether jitter originates before or after PipeWire;
* validating the PipeWire backend.

Prefer ALSA timestamped RawMIDI reads.

Configure:

```text
timestamped input
CLOCK_MONOTONIC_RAW
```

Conceptually use ALSA functionality equivalent to:

```text
SND_RAWMIDI_READ_TSTAMP
SND_RAWMIDI_CLOCK_MONOTONIC_RAW
snd_rawmidi_tread()
```

Do not merely:

```text
read MIDI byte
→ Instant::now()
```

unless timestamped RawMIDI is unavailable.

