# 14. ALSA fallback timestamping

If timestamped RawMIDI is unsupported, optionally support:

```text
clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC_RAW)
```

immediately after receiving the byte.

However:

1. print a prominent warning;
2. store the timestamp method in capture metadata;
3. label the result as userspace-timestamped;
4. never silently fall back;
5. do not compare it as equivalent to kernel timestamping without warning.

Never use:

```text
CLOCK_REALTIME
SystemTime
UTC time
wall clock
```

for jitter calculations.

