# 15. Backend comparison

A major eventual feature is comparing the two measurement layers.

Example:

```text
hardware source
       │
       ├──── ALSA RawMIDI measurement
       │
       └──── PipeWire measurement
```

Typical interpretation:

```text
ALSA phase RMS       0.35 ms
PipeWire phase RMS   0.38 ms
```

suggests little additional variability at the PipeWire application boundary.

Whereas:

```text
ALSA phase RMS       0.35 ms
PipeWire phase RMS   1.80 ms
```

would justify further investigation.

Do not assume that the difference between these two numbers can automatically be interpreted as "PipeWire jitter" unless both captures can be synchronized appropriately.

Independent capture runs include source variability.

