# 26. Primary jitter metrics

Report phase jitter and period jitter separately.

## Phase error

```text
phase_error[n]
    = measured_time[n] - ideal_time[n]
```

Report:

```text
mean
standard deviation
RMS
mean absolute error
median absolute error
P95 absolute error
P99 absolute error
earliest / minimum
latest / maximum
peak-to-peak
```

Units for presentation:

```text
milliseconds
```

Internal precision:

```text
nanoseconds or graph samples
```

## Period error

For adjacent valid clock ticks:

```text
measured_period[n]
    = t[n] - t[n-1]

period_error[n]
    = measured_period[n] - T
```

Report:

```text
mean interval
standard deviation
RMS period error
minimum interval
maximum interval
P95 absolute period error
P99 absolute period error
```

Intervals spanning inferred missing ticks must not be treated as normal one-tick intervals.

---

# 27. Phase versus period jitter

Do not conflate them.

Example A:

```text
phase:
+1 ms
+1 ms
+1 ms
+1 ms
```

This represents a phase offset but essentially no period instability.

Example B:

```text
phase:
+1 ms
-1 ms
+1 ms
-1 ms
```

This has much stronger tick-to-tick period variation.

Both metrics are required.

