# 38. Audibility and interpretation

Do not claim that:

```text
2 ms F8 jitter
```

necessarily produces:

```text
2 ms note timing jitter
```

A receiving sequencer may implement:

```text
clock smoothing
PLL
tempo estimation
phase correction
buffering
```

which can significantly change how raw F8 jitter propagates to musical events.

Therefore the application measures:

> MIDI Clock timing stability at the selected Linux measurement boundary.

It does not directly measure audible timing performance.

Avoid categorical labels such as:

```text
audible
inaudible
good
bad
```

in v0.1.

Prefer raw numerical statistics.

---

# 39. USB/interface considerations

USB MIDI interfaces may deliver events in bursts or batches.

If PipeWire or ALSA reports events with equal or unusual timing:

* preserve the values exactly;
* do not artificially spread them;
* flag suspicious patterns if appropriate.

Such behaviour may itself be part of the system under test.

Do not attempt to mathematically subtract:

```text
USB transport delay
DIN serialization time
interface latency
PipeWire latency
```

Constant latency is removed naturally by the fitted clock intercept.

Variable latency is part of the observed jitter.

